{# IPsec with a pre-shared key: IKE version 1 and version 2 (appendix A 3.13
   and 3.20). Syntax: cmdref 4.13 and 7.2 to 7.4, and the README of the pack
   ("参照した資料": the Security Command Reference and the IKEv2 guide).

   Version 1: the proposal of IKE and the keepalive belong to the whole
   device, so every row of version 1 must ask for the same. A row with an
   identity gets a keyring and an ISAKMP profile of its own (a crypto map
   entry or the IPsec profile of a tunnel interface names it).
   Version 2: one proposal and one policy for the device (none where the
   rows leave the proposal to the device), one keyring, and an IKEv2 profile
   for each row.
   A row on a tunnel interface makes a transform set and a profile ("tunnel
   protection", interfaces.j2); a row of the style "policy" is one entry of
   a crypto map, with an access list made from its selectors. The entry is
   "<map> <number>" for a row named "<map>/<number>"; a row with another
   name (one that came from another vendor) goes into a map named after its
   interface, numbered 10, 20 and so on in the order of such rows. A peer
   "any" makes a dynamic map; such a row in transport mode is what protects
   the callers of an LNS (L2TP over IPsec; the row of L2TP names it). The
   names of the transform sets, the profiles, the keyrings and those lists
   are made here: the design data has none. #}
